{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L175-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom","kind":"structure","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L173-L175","doc":"Derived-atom record (placeholder marker for content block ref resolution) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:derived-atom","label":"def:derived-atom","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/derived-atom.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.isShellClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.isShellClosed","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L168-L170","doc":"An atom is shell-closed if no NF coefficient is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.demandIndices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.demandIndices","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L163-L166","doc":"The demand profile of an NF vector: the set of indices\nwhere the coefficient is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.confinement_universality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.confinement_universality","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L141-L159","doc":"**Confinement universality.**\n\nThe nucleon NF depends only on q and the quark flavor assignment,\nnot on photon polarization parameters (φ₀, φ₁, φ₀₁).\n\nProof: `crossingCoeffsWithPol` is defined to be `crossingCoeffs`\nregardless of the polarization argument; the crossing coefficients\nare determined entirely by the crossing type (discrete quark-flavor\ndata), which is independent of the continuous photon parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.crossingCoeffsWithPol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.crossingCoeffsWithPol","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**Polarization-parameterised crossing coefficients.**\n\nThe derivation chain `γγ → quarks → B₃ · crossings → nucleon NF`\nfactors through the discrete quark type assignment; the photon\nparameters only affect the first (pair-production) arrow.  The\nsecond arrow — the Hecke-algebraic step that computes crossing\ncoefficients — depends only on `CrossingType` and `q`.\n\nFormally: `crossingCoeffsWithPol ct pol` equals `crossingCoeffs ct`\nfor all polarization parameters `pol`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₀₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₀₁","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L125-L125","doc":"Joint (two-photon) polarization coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₁","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L123-L123","doc":"Second photon polarization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.φ₀","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L121-L121","doc":"First photon polarization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.PolarizationParams","kind":"structure","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L114-L125","doc":"**Photon polarization parameters** `(φ₀, φ₁, φ₀₁)`.\n\nIn the γγ → pair-production step, the two photons carry polarization\nparameters.  The confinement universality theorem asserts that these\nparameters do not affect the nucleon normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ne_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ne_identity","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L109-L110","doc":"The ne crossing is the identity (no interaction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ee_eq_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ee_eq_pp","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The ee crossing has the same coefficients as pp (EM repulsion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.pe_shift_eq_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.pe_shift_eq_nn","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L103-L104","doc":"The pe crossing has the same 𝟙-shift as nn (EM attraction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.pn_sigma_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.pn_sigma_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The pn crossing σ-coefficient is 2 (doubled to stay in ℤ[q,q⁻¹]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.nn_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.nn_shift","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The nn crossing has identity shift −HA = −(q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.pp_no_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.pp_no_shift","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L94-L95","doc":"The pp crossing coefficient is just σ (no identity shift). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.crossingCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.crossingCoeffs","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L70-L92","doc":"The typed crossing element.\nReturns (σ-coefficient, 𝟙-coefficient) in ℤ[q, q⁻¹].\n\nNuclear:\n  pp: (1, 0)          — pure positive crossing (Coulomb repulsion)\n  nn: (1, −HA)        — Hecke inverse crossing (strong force)\n  pn: (2, −HA)        — averaged mixed crossing, stored as 2× to stay in ℤ[q,q⁻¹]\n\nElectron (POSTULATES — not derived from the Hecke algebra):\n  pe: (1, −HA)        — EM attraction (same as nn)\n  ne: (0, 1)          — no interaction (identity)\n  ee: (1, 0)          — EM repulsion (same as pp)\n\nNote: The electron crossing assignments map EM attraction/repulsion\nto the same algebraic structure as strong-force crossings. This is\na modeling ansatz, not a derivation. See discussion in PR #349. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.crossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.crossingType","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L56-L66","doc":"Determine crossing type from particle pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instReprCrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instReprCrossingType","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instReprCrossingType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instReprCrossingType.repr","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instDecidableEqCrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instDecidableEqCrossingType","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.ee","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.ee","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.ne","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pe","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pn","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.nn","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType.pp","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.CrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.CrossingType","kind":"inductive","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L36-L54","doc":"Inter-particle crossing type.\n\nNuclear crossings:\npp — proton-proton: σ (Coulomb repulsion)\nnn — neutron-neutron: σ⁻¹ (strong force)\npn — proton-neutron: ½(σ + σ⁻¹) (mixed)\n\nElectron crossings:\npe — proton-electron: σ⁻¹ (EM attraction, same coeffs as nn)\nne — neutron-electron: 𝟏 (no interaction)\nee — electron-electron: σ (EM repulsion, same coeffs as pp) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.NucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.NucleonType","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L33-L34","doc":"Legacy alias for backward compatibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instReprParticleType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instReprParticleType.repr","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instReprParticleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instReprParticleType","kind":"instance","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.instDecidableEqParticleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.instDecidableEqParticleType","kind":"instance","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.electron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.electron","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.neutron","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ParticleType.proton","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ParticleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ParticleType","kind":"inductive","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DerivedAtom.lean#L26-L31","doc":"A particle type: proton, neutron, or electron. ","signatureChunk":0}]}